    "text": "A motorcycle starts from rest and accelerates along a straight path at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. At the starting point, there was a siren which produced sound at a constant frequency. How far has the motorcycle gone from the starting point, If now the rider hears the frequency of the siren at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>94</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of its value as compared to when the motorcycle was rest? (Speed =&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>330</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"
